  "source": "Carlo Gavazzi EM21 Communication Protocol, version 1 revision 0 (7 April 2008)",
  "notes": [
    "Carlo Gavazzi EM21 (72 mm DIN, AV5 and AV6 input models).",
    "Values are read with function 03 or 04; at most 11 registers per request. 32-bit values are low word first (word order little).",
    "The manual also lists an identification code (57 = AV5, 58 = AV6) at address 0x000B, which overlaps the second word of V L3-L1, so it is left out.",
    "The manual's value weights: voltage x10, current x1000, power x10, power factor x1000, frequency x10, energy x10. An INT32 whose high word is 0x7FFF means overflow (the display shows ----).",
    "The programming (settings) tables of the manual are not in this map. Not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
